{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20148",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.59,
      "end_seconds": 3.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "Hello, good to see you. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 5.17,
      "end_seconds": 10.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.94,
      "end_seconds": 13.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "Where shall we begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.22,
      "end_seconds": 21.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "It's numbness in my fingers, doctor. He didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.26,
      "end_seconds": 26.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.07,
      "end_seconds": 32.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Probably about three months. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.38,
      "end_seconds": 43.58,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.4,
      "end_seconds": 64.08,
      "duration_seconds": 19.68,
      "text": "About a three out of ten. Honestly, on and off. I've also had tingling in my thumb and first two fingers, for about three months. As for tingling in my thumb and first two fingers, pretty mild, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.49,
      "end_seconds": 67.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Have you had dropping things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 69.7,
      "end_seconds": 71.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.89,
      "end_seconds": 80.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any injury to the wrist or swelling of the wrist?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.26,
      "end_seconds": 89.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "No injury to the wrist or swelling of the wrist, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.23,
      "end_seconds": 93.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Any weakness in the legs?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.45,
      "end_seconds": 100.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any weakness in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.73,
      "end_seconds": 102.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.46,
      "end_seconds": 107.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 109.11,
      "end_seconds": 113.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.99,
      "end_seconds": 124.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.11,
      "end_seconds": 134.75,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, is your urine normal, no changes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.26,
      "end_seconds": 136.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.28,
      "end_seconds": 150.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.59,
      "end_seconds": 155.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "I'm allergic to naproxen, I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.04,
      "end_seconds": 160.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "What does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.55,
      "end_seconds": 166.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.24,
      "end_seconds": 168.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Have you retired yet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.82,
      "end_seconds": 178.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "I retired from the post office two years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.18,
      "end_seconds": 182.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.64,
      "end_seconds": 185.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "My grandmother had dementia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 187.07,
      "end_seconds": 190.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.16,
      "end_seconds": 196.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "I have an underactive thyroid, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.4,
      "end_seconds": 198.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "And besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.01,
      "end_seconds": 202.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Diabetes, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.19,
      "end_seconds": 207.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 208.3,
      "end_seconds": 213.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "It's metformin, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.17,
      "end_seconds": 219.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "I used to take Eltroxin, but I stopped it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.79,
      "end_seconds": 229.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.05,
      "end_seconds": 234.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Just part of my thyroid removed, years back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 235.35,
      "end_seconds": 246.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.35,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. SpO2 99 percent on room air, blood pressure 124 over 77, temp 36.5 degrees, heart rate 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.34,
      "end_seconds": 248.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.7,
      "end_seconds": 253.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.4,
      "end_seconds": 258.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "Take a deep breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.97,
      "end_seconds": 279.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.19,
      "text": "Tapping over the wrist brings on the tingling, and the muscle at the base of the thumb looks slightly thin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.4,
      "end_seconds": 299.78,
      "duration_seconds": 17.38,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Okay, so my impression is this: My working impression is carpal tunnel syndrome. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Diabetic nerve damage is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.56,
      "end_seconds": 302.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.4,
      "end_seconds": 311.45,
      "duration_seconds": 7.05,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with carpal tunnel syndrome do well once it's treated properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.48,
      "end_seconds": 350.11,
      "duration_seconds": 29.63,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange nerve conduction tests for hand numbness. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm sending you for blood tests because of numbness. A wrist splint at night will often settle it. Let's get you seen by occupational therapy, I'll arrange the letter. We'll catch up in six weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.27,
      "end_seconds": 354.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}